{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Tubal-cain.</b> He seasoned the craft of Cain. תובל is of the root תבלין (spices/seasoning): he seasoned and perfected the craft of Cain to make weapons for murderers." "<b>He sharpened every tool of bronze and iron.</b> He sharpened the craft of bronze and iron, as in ״יִלְטֹשׁ עֵינָיו לִי״ (Job 16). חרשׁ is not a noun form but a verb form, for it has a small qamatz and its accent is below — meaning: he sharpens and burnishes every tool of craft in bronze and iron." "<b>Naamah.</b> She was the wife of Noah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "Rashi calls קמץ קטן what is more commonly called qamatz qatan; the 'accent below' (טעמו למטה) means the stress falls on the final syllable (milra), confirming it as a verb."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:35.800292168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}